hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"350","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’, Al-Makhzoumi, and Ahmad bin Abdah told us. Ahmad said: He told us, and the other two said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, said: “The women of the believing women used to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the morning prayer, and then They will come out, clad in their cloaks, and they will not be recognized.” Ahmed added: Then he mentioned the sitting"
"351","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, I am Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us He invaded Khaybar and said: “Then we prayed the morning prayer in silence.”"
"352","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman Al-Muradi told me, Ibn Wahb told me, Usama bin Zaid told me, that Ibn Shihab told him, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz He was sitting on the pulpit, so he delayed the prayer a little, and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr said: Gabriel had informed Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, the time Prayer, and Omar said to him: I know what you are saying, and Urwa said: I heard Bashir bin Abi Masoud, saying: I heard Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Gabriel came down and told me the time for prayer, so I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed.” with him, then I prayed with him, and he counted five prayers with his fingers, and I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying the noon prayer when the sun had passed, and perhaps He delayed it when the heat became intense, and I saw him praying the afternoon prayer while the sun was high and white before it set in, so the man would stop praying. Then Dhu al-Hulayfah would come before sunset, and he would pray Maghrib when the sun was setting, and he would pray Isha’ when the horizon was dark, and perhaps he would delay it until The people gathered, and he prayed the Fajr prayer once while sitting, then he prayed another time and made it clear, then his prayer after that was in sitting until he died, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace be upon him, then he did not return until he left.” Abu Bakr said: This addition was not said by anyone except Usama bin Zaid in this report. All of this is an indication that the twilight is white and not red, because in the report: He performs the Isha prayer when the horizon is dark, but the horizon darkens only after... The disappearance of the whiteness that occurs after the redness disappears, because if the redness disappears, the whiteness remains after it, then the whiteness disappears and it becomes black. Horizon, and in the news of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then Bilal gave the call to prayer The evening prayer was when the whiteness of the day had passed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to establish the prayer, so he prayed."
"353","Muhammad bin Yahya and Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told us, they said: Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, Sadaqa bin Abd told us. Allah Al-Dimashqi, on the authority of Abu Wahb, who is Ubaid Allah ibn Ubaid Al-Kala’i, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Musa, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Jabir Bin Abdullah, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about the time for prayer. He mentioned a long hadith about the times of prayer in The two days and two nights, and he said on the first night: Then Bilal gave the call to prayer for the evening prayer when the whiteness of the day had passed, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to do so. He greeted him, established the prayer and prayed, and said on the second night: Then Bilal called the call to prayer for the evening prayer when the whiteness of the day had passed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, delayed it. And we slept, and then we slept several times, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and said: “The people have prayed and fallen asleep, and you are still in Prayer since you have been waiting for prayer.” Then he mentioned the hadith in its length."
"354","On the authority of Ammar bin Khaled Al-Wasiti, on the authority of Muhammad, who is Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Al-Wasiti, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The time of noon until the afternoon, and the time of the afternoon until the yellowing of the sun, “The time of Maghrib until the redness of twilight disappears, the time of Isha until midnight, and the time of the morning prayer until sunrise.” Abu Bakr said: If this wording was correct in this report, this report would have stated that the twilight is red, but this The word was used only by Muhammad ibn Yazid, although it was preserved from him. Rather, the companions of Shu’bah said in this report: The twilight bull is a place What, Muhammad bin Yazid said: the redness of the twilight. It was narrated by Bundar and Abu Musa. They said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Ja’far, narrated to us. It was narrated by Shu’bah. He said: I heard Qatada. He said: I heard Abu Ayyub. Al-Azdi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, mentioned the hadith, and they said in the report: Maghrib time unless the twilight bull falls, and they do not raise it."
"355","Muhammad bin Labid told us, Uqba told me, he said: Abu Dawud told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, Shu`bah said: He raised it once, and Bundar said: Like the hadith of the first. It was also narrated by Hisham al-Dastawi, on the authority of Qatada, and he narrated it. I dictated it before. He said: Until twilight disappears, and he did not say: bull or red. It was also narrated by Sa`id bin Abi Orouba, but he did not narrate it, and he did not mention red. It was also narrated by Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Shu’bah, and he did not mention Al-Humra, on the authority of Shu’bah. Abu Musa, Ibn Abi Adi, told us about them, on the authority of Shu`bah. H And Abu Musa, Ibn Abi Adi, also told us, on the authority of Saeed, both of them, on the authority of Qatada, so this hadith is authentic, and it does not contain any mention of redness. Abu Bakr said: It is obligatory to consider if it is not proven from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the twilight is redness, and it is proven from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. The beginning of the time for Isha is when twilight has disappeared. He should not pray Isha until the whiteness of the horizon has disappeared, because what is non-existent is Non-existent, until its existence is known with certainty. Unless it is known with certainty that the time for prayer has begun, prayer is not obligatory, and it is not permissible to perform the obligatory prayer until after Certainty that the obligation has been fulfilled. If the redness has disappeared and the whiteness is still present and has not disappeared, then the beginning of the time for the Isha prayer is doubtful and not certain, because Scientists have differed regarding twilight. Some of them said: redness, and some said: whiteness, and it has not been scientifically proven from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that The red twilight, and unless it is proven from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Muslims do not agree on it, then it is not obligatory to make prayer obligatory, unless he makes it obligatory. God, His Messenger, or the Muslims at a certain time, if there is whiteness on the horizon, and the scholars have disagreed regarding the obligation of the evening prayer. There is no proven report from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that prayer was obligatory at that time. So if the whiteness goes away and turns black, then it is agreed upon. The scholars affirmed the obligation of the evening prayer, so it is permissible at that time to perform the obligation of that prayer, and God knows best, with the validity of this wording that It was mentioned in the hadith of Abdullah bin Amr"
